{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; see "},{"code":"MaximalCliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P7CliquesE07maximalC0AD07MaximalC0VyxGyF","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cliques"}],"symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques.swift#L381","fileName":"MaximalCliques.swift"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximalCliques"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MaximalCliques"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"maximalCliques()"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()"]}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques","title":"Cliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[],"title":"Graph"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","abstract":[{"text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; see ","type":"text"},{"code":"MaximalCliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"maximalCliques()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","kind":"symbol"}}}